Healthy Brain Network (HBN), MRI
================================

Imaging data of the Child Mind Institute Healthy Brain Network: children
and adolescents (5 to 21 years) from the New York area, scanned at four
sites: Staten Island (Site-SI, 1.5T mobile scanner), Rutgers University
Brain Imaging Center (Site-RU), the CitiGroup Biomedical Imaging Center
(Site-CBIC) and the CUNY Advanced Science Research Center (Site-CUNY).

    Alexander LM, Escalera J, Ai L, et al. (2017) An open resource for
    transdiagnostic research in pediatric mental health and learning
    disorders. Sci Data 4:170181.
    https://doi.org/10.1038/sdata.2017.181

Imaging data are openly available. Phenotypic data require a data usage
agreement (LORIS) and are not included; `participants.tsv` merges the
basic tables of the four sites (column `site` added). The column
`Commercial_Use` tells whether the participant consented to commercial
use of their data.

Downloaded by brainspresso from s3://fcp-indi/data/Projects/HBN/MRI/.
Entities of field map file names were put in BIDS order
(`dir-PA_acq-fMRI` -> `acq-fMRI_dir-PA`), magnetization transfer pairs
renamed (`MT-on_PD` -> `mt-on_MTR`), and `EchoTime1`/`EchoTime2`
of phase difference maps were filled in from the magnitude images when
missing. Trace-weighted images computed by the scanner (`*TRACEW_dwi`)
have no gradient table and are listed in `.bidsignore`. Derivatives of
the bucket (ANTs outputs, not BIDS) are not included.
